<!-- Homepage FAQ Section -->
<section style="padding: 4rem 0; background: var(--color-surface-alt);">
  <div class="container" style="max-width: 850px;">
    <div class="section-header">
      <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      <p>Everything you need to know about our nationwide shingle roofing referral network:</p>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-list">
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-summary">Is American Shingle Co. a direct roofing contractor?</summary>
        <div class="faq-content">
          <p>No. American Shingle Co. is a nationwide consumer matching service that connects homeowners with independent, vetted, licensed, and insured roofing contractors in their area. All contracts, estimates, warranties, and construction work are executed directly between you and the fulfilling contractor.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-summary">How quickly will a roofing contractor contact me?</summary>
        <div class="faq-content">
          <p>During normal operating hours, partner roofing contractors typically reach out within 30 to 90 minutes of your phone call or online estimate request. For immediate assistance, call our toll-free line at (833) 348-0328.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-summary">How much does a new shingle roof cost on average?</summary>
        <div class="faq-content">
          <p>For an average 2,000 square foot single-family home, architectural asphalt shingle installation generally ranges from $8,200 to $13,800. Premium materials like metal, composite, or slate range from $16,000 to over $45,000 depending on material selection, slope pitch, and tear-off layers.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-summary">Are contractors in the network licensed and insured?</summary>
        <div class="faq-content">
          <p>Yes. Participating contractors are required to carry active general liability insurance, worker's compensation, and all necessary state and municipal licenses required by their local building department jurisdictions.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-summary">Does using this referral service cost me anything?</summary>
        <div class="faq-content">
          <p>No. Connecting with partner roofing contractors through American Shingle Co. is completely free to homeowners. You pay the contractor directly for the roofing installation services specified in your written agreement.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

